 Day 2 — AWS S3 + CloudFront + Storage Architecture

STAR approach interview questions….

1️⃣ You need to store large media files with cost optimization and automatic tiering. How will you use S3 storage classes + lifecycle rules?

2️⃣ A customer-facing website delivers images slowly to users across the globe. How will you design S3 + CloudFront for optimal performance?

3️⃣ An S3 bucket with sensitive data was accidentally made public. What immediate and long-term remediation steps will you take?

4️⃣ Your application requires versioning + replication across regions for DR. How will you design S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) securely?

5️⃣ You need to restrict access to S3 objects only to CloudFront and block all direct access. How will you configure OAC/OAI?

6️⃣ A data processing job must read millions of small objects from S3. How will you optimize performance and cost?

7️⃣ You need to audit exactly who accessed S3 objects and when. Which AWS logging services will you enable?

8️⃣ A partner must upload files to your bucket, but should not view or modify existing files. How will you design IAM + Bucket Policies?

9️⃣ S3 upload latency is high for large files. What optimizations (multipart upload, transfer acceleration) will you use?

🔟 You need a data lake design with ETL pipelines and structured query support. Which AWS services will you integrate with S3?

1️⃣1️⃣ Encryption must be enforced using customer-managed KMS keys (CMEK). How will you configure bucket policies + key policies?

1️⃣2️⃣ S3 replication is failing. What will you troubleshoot (IAM roles, KMS keys, object metadata, bucket versioning)?

1️⃣3️⃣ A bucket storing logs is rapidly growing. How will you optimize cost using prefixes, lifecycle tiers, and intelligent-tiering?

1️⃣4️⃣ You need to deliver private downloadable files securely to authenticated users with URL expiration. How will you use CloudFront signed URLs?

1️⃣5️⃣ You must build a serverless image-processing workflow triggered on S3 object uploads. Which AWS services will you combine?

